Consider the function $f(x)=\frac{|x-1|}{x+1}$ defined on the closed interval 
$\left[\frac{R-1}{R+1}, \frac{R+1}{R-1} \right]$. 


Taking derivatives, it is elementary to verify that $f(x)$ is increasing in the interval 
$1< x < \frac{R+1}{R-1}$, while it is decreasing in the interval $\frac{R-1}{R+1}< x <1$. 

Furthermore, noting that $f(1)=0$, it is direct that 
{\small
